@format 1
@id media-preview.common.completion-routing
@title Completion routing
@section Media preview
@area Common
@entry backend-outcome
@summary Trace a raised backend completion through viewer staleness/failure filtering and the preview engine that was selected before the request began.
@related media-preview.common.viewer-gate, media-preview.common.mpv-preview, media-preview.common.flyleaf-preview, media-preview.common.media-publication, media-preview.in-edit
@tag media
@tag preview
@tag common
@tag completion

@alias media-load = Cadroue.Media.LMediaLoad
@alias viewer = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PViewer

[backend-outcome] Raised backend outcome <input>
~ This starts when the background media loader reports a result.
[Technical explanation]
- LMediaLoadRaise invokes this viewer subscriber independently from other backend subscribers @ media-load.LMediaLoadRaise(...)
> completion-filter

[completion-filter] Viewer completion acceptance <decision>
~ The program checks viewer completion acceptance.
[Technical explanation]
- Capture the current viewer load serial, marshal the callback onto the viewer dispatcher, then compare lifetime, serial, and expected source path before accepting the outcome @ viewer.PViewerLoadHandle(...)
? "Viewer request is stale" > stale
? "Current backend failure or cancellation" > failed-status
? "Current backend success" > engine-route

[stale] Stale completion ignored <output>
~ This path ends with stale completion ignored.
[Technical explanation]
= The completion cannot replace current viewer state.

[failed-status] Unreadable media cargo publication <process>
~ The program reports that the selected media could not be read.
[Technical explanation]
- Build cargo containing the failed source and backend error, then synchronously raise PViewerMediaChange without committing PViewerSourcePath or media information @ viewer.PViewerLoadHandle(...)
  @ viewer.PViewerMediaRaise(...)
> map:media-preview.common.media-publication

[engine-route] Previously selected preview engine <decision>
~ The program checks previously selected preview engine.
[Technical explanation]
- Route successful media information according to pViewerMpvActive, which was set by PViewerEngineSelect before backend loading; PViewerEngineRead can request mpv only for a viewer whose PViewerEditEligible property is true @ viewer.PPlayerMediaApply(...)
  @ viewer.PViewerEngineRead(...)
  @ property viewer.PViewerEditEligible
? "mpv active" > map:media-preview.common.mpv-preview
? "Flyleaf active" > map:media-preview.common.flyleaf-preview
